  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe status strip gains a Report door next to the Debug info door (#1696).\nIt opens a small window:\n\n- A short title field.\n- Two buttons, \"Report a bug\" and \"Request a feature\". Each opens the\n  browser on a prefilled GitHub new-issue URL: the title, the body and the\n  `bug` / `enhancement` label are already typed.\n- A \"Copy screenshot\" button. It asks the shell for a picture of the whole\n  application window: egui's `ViewportCommand::Screenshot`, answered by the\n  native shell's capture module (`shell_window/capture.rs`, a second render\n  pass of the same frame into a private texture). The picture goes to the\n  clipboard. The user pastes it into the issue description and GitHub\n  uploads it.\n\nThe body embeds the Debug info report (#157), so both paths carry the same\nfields from one source. When no answer arrives, the copy names that in\nwords, in the status line.\n\nProvenance: the mechanism is egui's public capture contract. The maintainer\npointed at SolidCraft's report dialog for the shape only; their code was\nnot read and their look is not used.\n\nThe repository also gains `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/blank-issue.md` and\n`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml` (GitHub reads `blank_issues_enabled`\nonly from that path). The new glyph `act-report.png` is the Tabler Icons\n(MIT) `banner` glyph; its SVG master `assets/ui/svg/act-report.svg` sits\nwith our masters and `assets/ui/LICENSES.md` names Tabler as its source.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `report_tests.rs` (new, kittest): URL encoding; the prefilled URL shape;\n  the body content; the door open and a kind button filing the URL; the\n  typed title in the URL; a kind button asking the shell for the whole\n  window; the answer copying the picture and saying the word; the copy\n  after the window is closed; an answer for another token left alone; no\n  answer copying nothing. 10 tests.\n- `structural.rs`: the door sits on the status strip; no floating window is\n  open by default (pin kept).\n- `op_icon_table.rs`: the `Report` glyph is SVG-mastered and unique.\n- `cargo xtask icons --check`: 0 breaches.\n- The maintainer GUI-tested the debug build on 2026-11-17 and said it looks\n  good: door, window, browser open with the prefilled issue, and the\n  whole-window picture on the clipboard.\n- Quick gate on the final head is named in the ready comment below.\n\n## Not exercised here\n\n- Clipboard paste into GitHub in an automated test: the tests assert the\n  clipboard write, not GitHub. The maintainer's GUI test covered the paste\n  path.\n\nNote for the reviewer: this PR touches `.github/`, so `pr-test.yml` refuses\nit and the review builds locally (read, not built: the yellow\n`needs-maintainer` path).\n\nBranch merges origin/main at 16658f67b.\n\nChangelog: The status strip gained a Report door: it opens a prefilled GitHub issue and copies a whole-window screenshot to the clipboard (#1696, PR #1798)\n\nFixes #1696\n",
